  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nIssued 208 PM MDT SAT AUG 15 2026\nAn upper-level shortwave trough will continue to move east through \nthe Pacific Northwest and Northern Rockies Tuesday and early \nWednesday. Shower and thunderstorm chances will be limited to the \nhigher terrain of central Idaho as this passes through. This \ndisturbance will suppress the upper-level ridge building in the \nGreat Basin on these days, however Wednesday afternoon onward the \nridge will amplify over the area. As the Desert Southwest ridge \nbuilds, southwesterly flow aloft will overspread the region, \nincreasing temperatures and moisture gradually late week. \nAdditionally, models agree on a Pacific low pressure system slowly \nmoving onshore late week going into the weekend. This pattern will \nsupport the influx of monsoonal moisture once again, with shower and \nthunderstorm chances increasing by Friday and further Saturday.",
